# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# fz-mart TEST environment — copy to .env.test and fill in.
# Commit THIS file (.env.test.example); never commit .env.test.
#
# Values here OVERRIDE .env for the Playwright suite only. Anything you
# leave out falls back to .env, so only list what must differ.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required: a THROWAWAY database ───────────────────────────────
# The E2E suite writes to this DB on every run: it creates an OWNER admin
# user, upserts shipping zone 1, flips the `payments` settings group into
# MOCK mode, creates an E2E100 coupon, and races real checkouts that
# decrement stock. None of that may ever touch a store with real orders.
#
# Local MySQL 8 (this project's chosen setup):
#   1. Install MySQL 8 for Windows (installer or `winget install Oracle.MySQL`).
#   2. Create the database and a user for it:
#        CREATE DATABASE fz_mart_test;
#        CREATE USER 'fzmart_test'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'choose-a-password';
#        GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON fz_mart_test.* TO 'fzmart_test'@'localhost';
#        FLUSH PRIVILEGES;
#   3. Put the matching URL below.
#   4. Apply the schema:  npm run db:migrate:test
#
# The same database also backs the coupon concurrency test:
#   npm run test:coupon-race   (scripts/test-coupon-race.ts)
# which seeds its own fixtures, races 20 concurrent checkouts against a
# usage-limited coupon, and tears everything down again.
#
# The suite REFUSES to run if this points at a hosted/production host
# (tidbcloud.com, planetscale, rds.amazonaws.com, …) or matches the
# DATABASE_URL in .env — see tests/e2e/helpers/guard.ts.
DATABASE_URL="mysql://fzmart_test:choose-a-password@localhost:3306/fz_mart_test"

# ── Required: a THROWAWAY Redis ──────────────────────────────────
# THE RULE, no exceptions: every external connection a test run can reach must
# be local, a test-named resource, or a mock. There is no "acceptable" remote
# target for any of them.
#
# This entry used to record an accepted risk — leaving REDIS_URL unset so it
# fell back to .env, i.e. production Upstash, on the reasoning that the suite
# only cleared ephemeral `ratelimit:*` counters. That reasoning is withdrawn.
# It was wrong twice over: session.spec.ts deletes session keys and rewrites
# TTLs, and the `ratelimit:*` clears were never as harmless as claimed — they
# are unscoped KEYS+DEL sweeps that wipe the login and checkout counters for
# every user, resetting a live brute-force budget to zero.
#
# The deeper lesson is that the exemption was granted per-service, so each new
# integration had to be remembered separately. It is now enforced structurally:
# assertTestEnvironment() in tests/e2e/helpers/guard.ts validates DATABASE_URL,
# REDIS_URL, R2_BUCKET, MAIL_DELIVERY and SMS_PROVIDER from one declarative
# list, runs once in globalSetup, and has its own test (helpers/guard.spec.ts)
# asserting the run ABORTS on production-looking values.
#
# Redis holds sessions (admin + customer), the session indexes, server carts,
# rate-limit counters and the IP-block set. The suite writes to all of them.
#
# Local Redis on Windows: run it under WSL2, or use Memurai / a Docker
# container (`docker run -p 6379:6379 redis:7-alpine`).
#
# Database index 1 keeps test keys off the default DB even when a local Redis
# is shared with other local work — `FLUSHDB` in a test never touches DB 0.
REDIS_URL="redis://127.0.0.1:6379/1"

# ── Required: non-delivering integrations ────────────────────────
# Anything that reaches a third party on the suite's behalf must be inert.
# R2 has no local host to point at, so the BUCKET NAME must mark it disposable
# (it must contain test/e2e/dev/local) — otherwise a spec that uploads a
# product image writes into the live store's bucket.
R2_BUCKET="fz-mart-test"

# "inline" would send through the real SMTP server. Keep it mocked.
MAIL_DELIVERY="mock"

# SMS/OTP is not built yet. Set it now so the first adapter to land cannot
# text real customers during a test run.
SMS_PROVIDER="mock"
